# .claude/verify-commands.example — template for the verify-gate Stop hook.
#
# The baseline ships a Stop hook (.claude/hooks/verify-gate.sh) that is dormant
# by default. To enforce verification before Claude Code can finish a coding
# turn, copy this file:
#
#   cp .claude/verify-commands.example .claude/verify-commands
#
# then uncomment/add the commands your project defines (see package.json,
# Makefile, pyproject.toml — do not invent commands the repo does not define).
# One command per line; lines starting with # are ignored. Every command must
# exit 0 for the turn to end. The gate skips read-only turns (clean git tree)
# and gives up after 3 consecutive blocks so it can never loop forever.
#
# Node:
#npm run lint
#npm run typecheck
#npm test
#
# Python:
#ruff check .
#pytest
#
# Go:
#go vet ./...
#go test ./...
#
# Make:
#make lint
#make test
